<title>SOUTH KOREA: Ssangyong Motors limit up at opening.</title>
<headline>Ssangyong Motors limit up at opening.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in ailing Ssangyong Motors went limit up at Thursday's opening on a newspaper report that its German partner, Mercedes Benz, a unit of Daimler-Benz AG, had agreed to inject 160 billion won into the carmaker, brokers said.</p>
<p>But the company denied the report.  </p>
<p>Ssangyong Motors gained 250 won to 4,300 at 0040 GMT with heavy trading volume of 300,950 shares.</p>
<p>The domestic Chosun Ilbo newspaper said Ssangyong and Daimler-Benz had tentatively agreed on the capital injection because the German partner expected high marketability of Ssangyong's new sedan model, called the &quot;Chairman&quot;.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5647</p>
